{
  "id": "ALAS2-2026-3943",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2 2017.12 - ALAS2-2026-3943: important priority package update for gvfs",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-09-28 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-28 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-84268:\n\tA flaw was found in the SFTP backend in gvfs. When mounting a share and reading a file, a malicious SFTP server can cause read_reply() to process a length that exceeds the size requested by the client. The function does not verify the server-provided length against the allocated buffer size, causing the operation to write past the intended boundaries. This issue allows a malicious server to corrupt adjacent heap memory in the gvfsd-sftp process, resulting in a denial of service as the process aborts upon detecting the heap corruption or potentially allowing arbitrary code execution.\n",
